//
// The decode (aie2_decode.py) at 2 layers on NPU2, test_llama.py's default
// tier: up to 4 tokens per dispatch, on-chip lm_head, sampler and feedback,
// growing KV. Every token, its record's seed, the last token's final residual
// and the whole KV cache match the numpy oracle, from an empty cache, across
// dispatches with the NPU idle between them, into the cache's last rows, for
// a split dispatch, sampled, and for a prompt in batches. --synthetic-weights
// swaps the embedding table and the layers' own weights for seeded ones in
// the same layout; one case (skipped where data/ is missing) runs the above
// on the model's real layer 0 and 1 instead. 16 real layers are the
// extensive tier and the nightly component check.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, xrt_python_bindings, xrt_python_ctrl_scratchpad_bo
//
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %pytest %S/test_llama.py -m "not extensive"
